## Frequently Asked Questions

### Does Riaz Counseling have male therapists?

Riaz Counseling's published content identifies Tremain Denton, LPC; Gregorie Trant, LPC; and Tyler Lemmons, LMSW, as male therapists on its team. Contact the practice to confirm current availability and whether a particular clinician is accepting new clients.

### Who is the male therapist at Riaz Counseling for men's issues?

Tremain Denton, LPC, has men's issues specifically listed among his areas of expertise. His profile also includes anxiety, depression, coping skills, relationships, self-esteem, stress, and trauma-related concerns.

### Is it better for men to have a male therapist?

Not necessarily. Some men feel more comfortable working with a male therapist, while others prefer a female therapist or have no gender preference. The quality of the therapeutic relationship, professional qualifications, relevant experience, and communication are important considerations.

### What issues can men discuss in individual therapy?

Men can discuss a wide range of concerns, including anxiety, depression, stress, relationships, marriage, parenting, grief, trauma, work pressure, self-esteem, identity, and life transitions. Therapy can also provide support with personal growth and developing healthier coping strategies.

### Is men's counseling only for men with depression or anxiety?

No. Counseling is not limited to people with a mental health diagnosis. Someone may seek therapy to improve communication, work through a difficult experience, understand recurring relationship patterns, manage stress, or make an important life decision.

### Does Riaz Counseling offer in-person therapy for men in Houston?

Riaz Counseling lists in-person office locations in Houston Galleria, Sugar Land, and The Woodlands. Online therapy is also listed for people across Texas. Confirm the available formats and locations for your preferred provider before scheduling.

### Can I request a male counselor when scheduling?

Yes. You can tell the practice that you prefer a male therapist and ask which clinicians may be available. You can also ask about their credentials, areas of focus, therapeutic approaches, and appointment options before making a decision.

### What if I feel uncomfortable talking during my first session?

It is normal to feel uncertain when beginning therapy, especially if you are discussing personal concerns for the first time. You can start with the issue that feels easiest to explain, ask questions, and let your therapist know if you need time before discussing something more personal.

